%% Worked example: a morning-triage loop + a review loop sharing a memory file.
%% This is the kind of setup Part 6 upgrades into a real graph.
graph LR
    classDef loop fill:#fde68a,stroke:#92400e
    classDef checker fill:#bfdbfe,stroke:#1e3a8a
    classDef gate fill:#fecaca,stroke:#7f1d1d
    classDef anchor fill:#bbf7d0,stroke:#14532d
    classDef memory fill:#e5e7eb,stroke:#374151

    Triage[Loop: morning-triage]:::loop -->|produced| Spine[(MemoryFile: progress.md)]:::memory
    Triage -->|checked_by| Rev1{Checker: triage-reviewer}:::checker
    Rev1 -->|routes_to risky| Gate[[HumanGate: needs-a-human]]:::gate
    Rev1 -->|verified_against| Tests((Anchor: pytest exit_code)):::anchor

    Changelog[Loop: changelog-writer]:::loop -->|reads| Spine
    Changelog -->|produced| Notes[(MemoryFile: CHANGELOG.md)]:::memory
    Changelog -->|checked_by| Rev2{Checker: changelog-reviewer}:::checker

    %% CIRCLED: this finding lives only in a transcript today —
    %% "flaky test root-caused to tz_default_utc" was said out loud in a chat,
    %% never written into progress.md as a typed claim. Changelog loop cannot see it.

    %% CIRCLED: Triage has no watcher on "issues closed per day" —
    %% nothing catches it if the loop starts closing issues without real fixes (Gaming, Concept 12).
